WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.070
In Osaka, your page is in English,
with no way to choose Japanese.

2
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:10.810
Its text is plain JSX, and
the app has no i18n library.

3
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:16.210
General Translation lets
you add i18n with gt-next:

4
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.970
wrap text in T and generate translations.

5
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.730
Wrap your config in withGTConfig,
list your languages,

6
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.470
and add a file that
loads their translations.

7
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.030
Put the GTProvider in your
root layout, wrap text in T,

8
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.310
and add a LocaleSelector for the menu.

9
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.870
Run npx gt translate before next build
to write a file for each language.

10
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.810
In Osaka, the menu now offers
Spanish, French and Japanese,

11
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.030
and the reader picks Japanese.
